I successfully completed the Phishing Analysis Fundamentals room on TryHackMe, focusing on understanding email structures and
identifying phishing indicators through practical email forensics.

## Topics Learned
  #Email structure and components (headers, body, metadata)
  #Email routing and delivery process using Received headers
  #Email authentication mechanisms:
  #SPF (Sender Policy Framework)
  #DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail)
  #DMARC (Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting & Conformance)
  #Identifying X-Originating-IP and tracing message origin
  #Understanding Return-Path and Reply-To manipulation techniques
  #Recognizing phishing indicators in email content and headers
  #Understanding spam and phishing delivery techniques

##Techniques Used
  #Email header analysis and deep inspection
  #IP extraction and defanging for safe reporting
  #Header tracing to identify sender infrastructure
  #Verification of authentication results (SPF, DKIM, DMARC)
  #Cross-checking sender domain legitimacy
  #Identifying suspicious links, redirects, and unsubscribe traps
  #Email source code inspection (raw MIME analysis)
  #Threat indicator identification and classification

##Outcome

This exercise strengthened my ability to perform email forensics and phishing analysis, improving my skills in identifying malicious
emails, tracing their origin, and validating email authenticity. These are essential competencies for cybersecurity incident response 
and threat detection roles.
